Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Session resumed. Majority Leader.

asr-000775-split-2
00:49:39.800 --> 00:49:59.980
Rep. Patricia C. Calderon: Mr. Speaker, the parliamentary status of House Bill No. 10858 is that it is in the period of sponsorship and debate. I now move to consider the proposed budget of the Department of Foreign Affairs and its attached agencies.

asr-000776
00:50:00.000 --> 00:50:06.900
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: There is a motion. Any objection? There is none. Motion is carried. Majority Leader.

asr-000776-split-2
00:50:06.900 --> 00:50:29.980
Rep. Patricia C. Calderon: Mr. Speaker, may we acknowledge the presence of the heads and officials from the Department of Foreign Affairs, namely Secretary Maria Theresa P. Lazaro, Chief Coordinator Maria Antonina M. Mendoza-Oblena, Undersecretary Maria Theresa B. Dizon-De Vega, and Undersecretary Leo M. Herrera-Lim.

asr-000777
00:50:30.000 --> 00:50:42.440
Rep. Patricia C. Calderon: Undersecretary Maria Andrelita S. Austria, OIC Undersecretary Ezadin H. [unclear], and the other assistant secretaries.

asr-000777-split-2
00:50:42.440 --> 00:50:55.000
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: We acknowledge the presence of the heads and officials of the Department of Foreign Affairs, led by Secretary Maria Theresa P. Lazaro. Welcome to the House of Representatives. Maayong buntag. Majority Leader.

asr-000778
00:50:55.000 --> 00:51:22.120
Rep. Patricia C. Calderon: Mr. Speaker, I move to recognize Representative Sancho Fernando Oaminal of Misamis Occidental and Representative Niko Raul Daza of Northern Samar of the Committee on Appropriations to answer questions on the proposed budget of the Department of Foreign Affairs.

asr-000778-split-2
00:51:22.120 --> 00:51:29.980
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Vice Chair Sancho Fernando "Ando" Oaminal and Vice Chair Niko Raul Daza, you have the floor.

asr-000779
00:51:30.000 --> 00:51:59.980
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Mr. Speaker, distinguished colleagues, ladies and gentlemen, please allow me to welcome to the House of Representatives the Department of Foreign Affairs, headed by Secretary Maria Theresa P. Lazaro, together with its attached agencies: the Foreign Service Institute, the Presidential Commission on Visiting Forces, and the UNESCO National Commission of the Philippines. It is my honor, together with my colleague Representative Niko Raul Daza, to sponsor

asr-000780
00:52:00.000 --> 00:52:29.980
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: the DFA's proposed budget for fiscal year 2027 in the amount of approximately 35.17 billion. This represents a 21.77% increase from the fiscal year 2026 GAA and will support the department's work in national security, economic diplomacy, consular services, assistance to Filipinos overseas, and organizational development. Fellow

asr-000781
00:52:30.000 --> 00:52:59.980
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: members of Congress, the Department of Foreign Affairs plays a central role in advancing and protecting Philippine interests abroad. Its work remains anchored on the three pillars of Philippine foreign policy: preservation and enhancement of national security, promotion and attainment of economic security, and protection of the rights and promotion of the welfare and interests of Filipinos overseas. This year the Philippines has taken on a major regional responsibility as chair of ASEAN

asr-000782
00:53:00.000 --> 00:53:29.980
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: under the theme "Navigating Our Future, Together." Through our chairship, the Philippines has helped advance key regional priorities and would have hosted more than 640 meetings throughout the year at the leaders', ministerial, officials' and technical levels. A key outcome of the May 2026 summit in Cebu is the ASEAN Leaders' Declaration on Maritime Cooperation, which provides for

asr-000783
00:53:30.000 --> 00:53:59.980
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: the establishment of the ASEAN Maritime Center to be hosted by the Philippines. Beyond ASEAN, the department continues to strengthen the Philippines' bilateral and multilateral partnerships in pursuit of mutually beneficial cooperation. These engagements serve to build and strengthen alliances and partnerships, promote Philippine economic interests, particularly trade and investment, and strengthen people-to-people ties. Maritime security remains a major foreign policy priority.

asr-000784
00:54:00.000 --> 00:54:29.000
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: This year marked the tenth anniversary of the 2016 arbitral award. The 1982 United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea and the 2016 award remain the twin anchors of our foreign policy in the maritime space as we protect and promote our sovereignty, sovereign rights and jurisdiction in the West Philippine Sea. Mr. Speaker, service to our Filipinos overseas remains at the core of the department's work. This

asr-000813
00:54:29.000 --> 00:54:33.660
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: responsibility has become even more important amid continuing conflict in the Middle East.

asr-000814
00:54:33.660 --> 00:54:40.160
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: The DFA, through our foreign service posts, continues to assist Filipinos affected by hostilities

asr-000815
00:54:40.160 --> 00:54:45.640
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: and coordinates closely with the Department of Migrant Workers and other partner agencies

asr-000816
00:54:45.640 --> 00:54:48.760
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: on repatriation and other forms of assistance.

asr-000817
00:54:49.780 --> 00:54:55.600
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: The Department continues its diplomatic engagements with governments and international organizations

asr-000818
00:54:55.600 --> 00:55:00.580
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: to help safeguard Filipino seafarers and Philippine-flagged vessels

asr-000819
00:55:00.580 --> 00:55:05.440
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: operating in areas affected by conflict and heightened security risks.

asr-000820
00:55:06.160 --> 00:55:11.020
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: These efforts underscore the need for the Department to maintain the capability to respond quickly

asr-000821
00:55:11.020 --> 00:55:15.040
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: whenever the safety and welfare of Filipinos overseas are at risk.

asr-000822
00:55:15.800 --> 00:55:19.540
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: The DFA likewise continues to work closely with the Department of Migrant Workers

asr-000823
00:55:19.540 --> 00:55:21.740
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: in serving Filipinos overseas.

asr-000824
00:55:22.420 --> 00:55:25.260
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: In countries without a resident migrant workers' office,

asr-000825
00:55:25.600 --> 00:55:30.160
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: the DFA continues to play a lead role in looking after our Kababayans.

asr-000826
00:55:30.700 --> 00:55:34.320
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: The Department also remains responsible for overseas Filipinos

asr-000827
00:55:34.320 --> 00:55:36.880
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: who are not classified as migrant workers,

asr-000828
00:55:37.500 --> 00:55:42.520
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: including students, tourists, permanent residents, and other Filipino nationals.

asr-000829
00:55:43.000 --> 00:55:47.500
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: At the same time, the Department continues to bring consular services closer to the public.

asr-000830
00:55:47.500 --> 00:55:52.800
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: In 2026, the DFA processed more than 1.5 million passports,

asr-000831
00:55:53.480 --> 00:55:55.260
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: issued hundreds of thousands,

asr-000832
00:55:55.600 --> 00:56:03.040
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: and continued to provide services through its 42 consular offices nationwide.

asr-000833
00:56:03.600 --> 00:56:09.620
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: The 2027 budget will support preparations for the next-generation Philippine passport,

asr-000834
00:56:10.120 --> 00:56:13.120
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: which is expected to feature enhanced security features,

asr-000835
00:56:13.740 --> 00:56:16.100
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: updated contactless chip technology,

asr-000836
00:56:16.520 --> 00:56:19.900
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: and an option for additional passport pages.

asr-000837
00:56:19.900 --> 00:56:23.920
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: It will likewise support continued investments in ICT,

asr-000838
00:56:24.940 --> 00:56:25.440
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: cybersecurity,

asr-000839
00:56:25.600 --> 00:56:27.600
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: and data protection.

asr-000840
00:56:27.600 --> 00:56:31.040
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: The DFA is also expanding the reach of the Foreign Service

asr-000841
00:56:31.040 --> 00:56:34.360
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: through the opening of new posts in strategic locations,

asr-000842
00:56:34.360 --> 00:56:39.320
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: including our embassies in Accra, Ghana, and Astana, Kazakhstan,

asr-000843
00:56:39.320 --> 00:56:41.960
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: which are expected to open this year,

asr-000844
00:56:41.960 --> 00:56:45.240
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: and our Consulate General in Miami, Florida,

asr-000845
00:56:45.240 --> 00:56:47.740
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: which is scheduled for 2027.

asr-000846
00:56:47.740 --> 00:56:52.320
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: These posts will help bring services closer to Filipino communities abroad

asr-000847
00:56:52.320 --> 00:56:55.580
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: while strengthening the country's political and economic engagement.

asr-000848
00:56:55.600 --> 00:56:58.600
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Mr. Speaker, distinguished colleagues,

asr-000849
00:56:59.380 --> 00:57:04.780
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: the DFA's proposed fiscal year 2027 budget will support its core operations

asr-000850
00:57:04.780 --> 00:57:08.880
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: and respond to the Philippines' growing requirements in national security,

asr-000851
00:57:09.580 --> 00:57:12.040
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: economic diplomacy, consular services,

asr-000852
00:57:12.740 --> 00:57:14.400
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: assistance to overseas Filipinos,

asr-000853
00:57:14.840 --> 00:57:16.500
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: and its organizational development.

asr-000854
00:57:17.500 --> 00:57:22.100
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Given the Department's important role in advancing Philippine interests on the global stage,

asr-000855
00:57:22.100 --> 00:57:25.580
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: I respectfully urge this House to support the DFA's mission to improve the country's economic development,

asr-000856
00:57:25.600 --> 00:57:26.720
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: and provide the approval of the proposed

asr-000857
00:57:26.860 --> 00:57:29.280
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: fiscal year 2027 budget of the Department of Foreign Affairs

asr-000858
00:57:29.280 --> 00:57:31.920
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: and its attached agencies.

asr-000859
00:57:31.920 --> 00:57:33.800
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Thank you very much, Mr. Speaker.

asr-000860
00:57:34.020 --> 00:57:37.600
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Salamat kay Cong Ando. Majority Leader.

asr-000861
00:57:38.320 --> 00:57:40.320
Rep. Patricia C. Calderon: Mr. Speaker, I move to recognize

asr-000862
00:57:41.240 --> 00:57:43.200
Rep. Patricia C. Calderon: Representative Presley DeJesus

asr-000863
00:57:43.200 --> 00:57:44.800
Rep. Patricia C. Calderon: of Phil Recca Party List

asr-000864
00:57:45.640 --> 00:57:47.580
Rep. Patricia C. Calderon: to Interpolate the Sponsor and the proposed budget

asr-000865
00:57:47.580 --> 00:57:49.080
Rep. Patricia C. Calderon: of the Department of Foreign Affairs.

asr-000866
00:57:49.080 --> 00:57:50.660
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: The gentleman from Phil Recca,

asr-000867
00:57:50.660 --> 00:57:51.600
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Party List

asr-000868
00:57:51.600 --> 00:57:52.360
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Honorable Presley

asr-000869
00:57:52.360 --> 00:57:53.000
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: DeJesus,

asr-000870
00:57:53.000 --> 00:57:53.500
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Sir,

asr-000871
00:57:53.500 --> 00:57:54.920
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: You are recognized

asr-000872
00:57:54.920 --> 00:57:55.580
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: to interpolate the sponsor and the proposed budget of the Department of Foreign Affairs.

asr-000873
00:57:55.580 --> 00:58:05.140
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Mr. Speaker. May the good gentleman, the good sponsor, yield some questions from this representation.

asr-000874
00:58:06.460 --> 00:58:07.620
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: The gentleman, if he's ready.

asr-000875
00:58:08.280 --> 00:58:09.500
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Willingly so, Mr. Speaker.

asr-000876
00:58:09.820 --> 00:58:10.320
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you.

asr-000877
00:58:10.540 --> 00:58:11.120
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Please proceed.

asr-000878
00:58:11.900 --> 00:58:13.920
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Good morning, Mr. Speaker, distinguished sponsor.

asr-000879
00:58:13.920 --> 00:58:34.100
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Let me start by returning to the previous discussions during the committee briefings that DFA reported then that 44.5 million had been appropriated for online voting and overseas voter registration information campaigns.

asr-000880
00:58:35.000 --> 00:58:37.760
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: This is for 2027 fiscal year.

asr-000881
00:58:38.920 --> 00:58:39.560
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Am I right?

asr-000882
00:58:40.140 --> 00:58:40.740
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Is this correct?

asr-000883
00:58:41.580 --> 00:58:42.420
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Yes, Mr. Speaker.

asr-000884
00:58:43.920 --> 00:58:51.140
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Yet, records would show that turnout remains low during recent years.

asr-000885
00:58:51.900 --> 00:58:52.500
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Is this correct?

asr-000886
00:58:53.800 --> 00:58:55.200
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: That's correct, Mr. Speaker.

asr-000887
00:58:55.900 --> 00:58:57.840
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: May I know what's the reason behind?

asr-000888
00:58:58.540 --> 00:59:01.960
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: How come the turnout remains so low from previous years?

asr-000889
00:59:02.200 --> 00:59:08.600
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Mr. Speaker, maraming factors to consider bakit medyo mababa yung turnout.

asr-000890
00:59:08.600 --> 00:59:12.600
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: And a few of which are the mobility of overseas Filipinos.

asr-000891
00:59:13.200 --> 00:59:13.800
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Work relationships.

asr-000892
00:59:13.920 --> 00:59:14.860
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Related constraints.

asr-000893
00:59:15.240 --> 00:59:17.540
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Minsan, hindi po pinapayagan ng mga employees nila.

asr-000894
00:59:18.160 --> 00:59:21.360
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Country-specific restrictions and geographic dispersion.

asr-000895
00:59:21.880 --> 00:59:24.660
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Political engagement or lack of confidence.

asr-000896
00:59:25.660 --> 00:59:28.880
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: And we have a limited awareness of the registration and the process.

asr-000897
00:59:29.260 --> 00:59:42.320
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Yung iba po nating kababayan, hirap po sila to participate kasi hindi po nila alam yung how to go about it and how to participate in the electoral procedure, Mr. Speaker.

asr-000898
00:59:42.320 --> 00:59:45.320
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Mr. Speaker, this is your sponsor.

asr-000899
00:59:45.600 --> 00:59:47.460
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: You mentioned lack of confidence.

asr-000900
00:59:48.400 --> 00:59:50.400
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Can you elaborate what does it mean?

asr-000901
00:59:53.700 --> 00:59:57.820
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Mr. Speaker, lack of confidence.

asr-000902
00:59:57.820 --> 00:59:58.920
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Mr. Speaker, lack of confidence.

asr-000903
01:00:00.000 --> 01:00:21.060
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: When I say lack of confidence po, Mr. Speaker, ibig sabihin po, yung mga workers po, they are not that confident yet in the process by which the elections is being done.

asr-000904
01:00:21.060 --> 01:00:42.120
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: They need more awareness, Mr. Speaker, kaya po yung Department of Foreign Affairs are consistently undergoing trainings and information campaigns to educate better these intended participants of the electoral process, Mr. Speaker.

asr-000905
01:00:42.120 --> 01:00:49.500
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So in short, the lack of confidence, when you translate that to Tagalog, it means wala silang tiwala? Ganun ba yun?

asr-000906
01:00:50.080 --> 01:00:51.040
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Sa proseso?

asr-000907
01:00:51.060 --> 01:01:09.280
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: So, it's not na wala po silang tiwala, Mr. Speaker, pero in a way din po, parang some of them feel that their votes do not necessarily make an impact, kaya hindi na lang po sila bumuboto.

asr-000908
01:01:09.280 --> 01:01:21.040
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: So they need more awareness and more information campaigns po, Mr. Speaker. Kumbaga, kailangan po ipaintindi po sa kanila na every vote counts.

asr-000909
01:01:21.060 --> 01:01:25.000
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Mr. Speaker, Distinguished Sponsor.

asr-000910
01:01:25.900 --> 01:01:32.260
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: How much funds were allocated in the previous years for overseas absentee voting?

asr-000911
01:01:33.000 --> 01:01:49.080
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: And in connection to that, could you explain the reasons for this low voter turnout and if this is isolated only in specific jurisdictions or is this prevalent in all countries where we have overseas voters?

asr-000912
01:01:51.060 --> 01:02:00.600
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Mr. Speaker, we are just gathering the data in terms of yung amount expended in the previous years.

asr-000913
01:02:01.200 --> 01:02:08.920
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: But for the turnout, it seems to be consistent in the different regions of the world.

asr-000914
01:02:09.820 --> 01:02:20.600
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Sa highest po is only 24.16%, which is in the Asia and the Pacific, and the lowest is in North and Latin Americas, which is 7.9%.

asr-000915
01:02:21.060 --> 01:02:28.680
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: And as I've mentioned earlier, Mr. Speaker, maraming factors po ang nag-contribute due to the low turnout.

asr-000916
01:02:28.920 --> 01:02:39.320
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: But the department is already doubling its efforts, ensuring that in the next electoral process, this will greatly improve, Mr. Speaker.

asr-000917
01:02:40.440 --> 01:02:47.060
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Have you tried the COMLEC na magkaroon kayo ng consultation or technical working group when it comes to this?

asr-000918
01:02:47.860 --> 01:02:50.060
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: At least, are they involved, COMLEC?

asr-000919
01:02:50.060 --> 01:02:50.660
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: COMLEC?

asr-000920
01:02:51.060 --> 01:02:56.840
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Yes, definitely, Mr. Speaker. The COMLEC is very much involved in this procedure.

asr-000921
01:02:58.840 --> 01:03:08.760
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: My follow-up question, just to put this in context, how many overseas registered voters do we have in 2025, if we have the figures on hand?

asr-000922
01:03:08.760 --> 01:03:19.800
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: As of 2025, Mr. Speaker, there are 1,241,690 registered overseas voters, to be exact po.

asr-000923
01:03:20.600 --> 01:03:21.000
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Out of?

asr-000924
01:03:21.060 --> 01:03:26.560
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Out of this 1.2 million voters, how many had actually voted?

asr-000925
01:03:27.580 --> 01:03:37.500
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Out of the 1.2 million po, Mr. Speaker, 228,000 approximately were able to actually vote, which is equivalent to 18.4%, Mr. Speaker.

asr-000926
01:03:37.860 --> 01:03:40.800
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, napakababa pala ng turnout natin.

asr-000927
01:03:41.460 --> 01:03:42.280
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Yes, Mr. Speaker.

asr-000928
01:03:42.640 --> 01:03:45.180
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Almost 18%, Mr. Speaker.

asr-000929
01:03:45.180 --> 01:03:49.560
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, ano sa tingin mo ang reason neto?

asr-000930
01:03:49.740 --> 01:03:50.180
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Because you mentioned ago...

asr-000931
01:03:51.060 --> 01:03:55.980
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Lack of confidence, kailangan you have a massive information campaign.

asr-000932
01:03:57.040 --> 01:04:05.220
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Internet voting removed the physical distance problem, but turnout was still only about 18% among OBCS voters.

asr-000933
01:04:05.220 --> 01:04:09.240
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, what does DFA's post-election assessment say?

asr-000934
01:04:09.880 --> 01:04:20.180
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Were the actual barriers pre-voting enrollment, digital literacy, authentication, awareness, trust, connectivity, or something else?

asr-000935
01:04:20.320 --> 01:04:21.020
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Or maybe?

asr-000936
01:04:21.060 --> 01:04:25.660
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Yung mga kababayan ba natin, natatakot sila because they're not documented?

asr-000937
01:04:27.780 --> 01:04:36.840
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Several factors mentioned by the good gentleman, Mr. Speaker, contributed po dun sa low turnout.

asr-000938
01:04:37.420 --> 01:04:42.080
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: And yung digital literacy is very important din po.

asr-000939
01:04:42.080 --> 01:04:50.080
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Isa yun sa malaking reason bakit po hindi nakaboto.

asr-000940
01:04:50.080 --> 01:04:53.640
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Nakaboto yung iba nating kababayan kahit na gusto po nilang bumoto.

asr-000941
01:04:53.640 --> 01:05:10.120
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: And that is why in the past several months and in the upcoming months, nagkaroon at magkakaroon po yung DFA ng overseas regional training for continuing overseas voter registration.

asr-000942
01:05:10.620 --> 01:05:17.640
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Kasama na din po dyan yung process by which on how to exercise their vote, Mr. Speaker.

asr-000943
01:05:17.640 --> 01:05:21.420
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Mr. Speaker, Distinguished Sponsor,

asr-000944
01:05:21.420 --> 01:05:33.260
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: I understand that statutory division of responsibility, but DFA operates the foreign service post and undertook information registration activities.

asr-000945
01:05:34.160 --> 01:05:40.300
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: I therefore want DFA's own expenditures and outputs separated from COMELEC.

asr-000946
01:05:40.300 --> 01:05:46.660
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Besides, Mr. Speaker, overseas registration for the succeeding election cycle,

asr-000947
01:05:47.640 --> 01:05:57.440
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: already began on December 1, 2025, and is scheduled to continue through September 30, 2027 at embassies and consulates.

asr-000948
01:05:58.060 --> 01:06:02.940
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So I presume we'll be funding these activities again. Am I right?

asr-000949
01:06:04.400 --> 01:06:11.560
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Yes, Mr. Speaker. Nakahiwalay po talaga yung budget ng overseas voting under the DFA.

asr-000950
01:06:11.560 --> 01:06:16.560
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: For 2026, nagkaroon po ng 44.4 million separately.

asr-000951
01:06:17.640 --> 01:06:19.640
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: For that purpose.

asr-000952
01:06:19.860 --> 01:06:27.600
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: And iba din po yung budget allocated by the COMELEC, which I do not have any record for.

asr-000953
01:06:27.700 --> 01:06:28.920
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: This office does not have any record.

asr-000954
01:06:29.020 --> 01:06:33.120
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So yung sa COMELEC, so you have separate budget with COMELEC. Am I right?

asr-000955
01:06:33.420 --> 01:06:34.280
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Yes, Mr. Speaker.

asr-000956
01:06:34.320 --> 01:06:36.400
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So paano nyo nire-reconcile yun?

asr-000957
01:06:36.740 --> 01:06:38.160
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Wala bang duplicity?

asr-000958
01:06:38.600 --> 01:06:41.000
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Mga mamiya, nag-fund kayo, ganun din sila.

asr-000959
01:06:41.000 --> 01:06:47.620
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So there will be a separate, may kanya-kanya, baka yung jurisdiction, or how to go.

asr-000960
01:06:47.700 --> 01:06:48.080
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: About it?

asr-000961
01:06:48.880 --> 01:06:56.520
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Mr. Speaker, as to the details of the budget, kasi part of which is the traveling expenses.

asr-000962
01:06:57.300 --> 01:07:02.480
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: So yung mga officials po ng COMELEC, dun po nila sinacharge sa office nila sa DFA naman po.

asr-000963
01:07:02.580 --> 01:07:05.740
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Dito naman po under the DFA training expenses din po.

asr-000964
01:07:07.140 --> 01:07:11.360
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Training of, there's a counterpart of DFA and there's a counterpart of COMELEC.

asr-000965
01:07:11.360 --> 01:07:17.360
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: So we assure the good gentleman that there is no duplicity.

asr-000966
01:07:17.640 --> 01:07:20.460
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Of the expenses, Mr. Chair.

asr-000967
01:07:21.360 --> 01:07:22.500
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Thank you, Mr. Sponsor.

asr-000968
01:07:23.320 --> 01:07:28.220
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Mr. Speaker, before we fund further preparatory activity in 2027,

asr-000969
01:07:29.160 --> 01:07:36.740
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: when will Congress receive the costed proposal for the hybrid or revised overseas voting system,

asr-000970
01:07:37.240 --> 01:07:40.360
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: including lessons learned from 2025?

asr-000971
01:07:40.360 --> 01:07:51.620
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: I'm sorry, may we repeat the question, Mr. Speaker?

asr-000972
01:07:51.620 --> 01:08:02.580
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Again, before we fund further preparatory activity for 2027, right now, because asking for another fund for 2027 here in Congress,

asr-000973
01:08:03.580 --> 01:08:09.360
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: kailan namin matatanggap yung costed proposal for the hybrid or revised overseas voting system,

asr-000974
01:08:09.880 --> 01:08:10.340
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: including lessons learned from 2025?

asr-000975
01:08:10.340 --> 01:08:12.560
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Kailan namin matatanggap yung lessons learned from 2025?

asr-000976
01:08:12.780 --> 01:08:16.940
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Remember 2025, the turnout was only around 18%.

asr-000977
01:08:16.940 --> 01:08:19.640
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: 18% lang, Mr. Chair.

asr-000978
01:08:20.060 --> 01:08:22.120
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: The actual votes, right?

asr-000979
01:08:22.500 --> 01:08:30.580
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So ngayon, 2027, yung costing nyo for the preparation for the hybrid or revised overseas voting system.

asr-000980
01:08:31.240 --> 01:08:37.600
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So anong gagawin natin na hindi natin maulit yung turnout natin na 18%?

asr-000981
01:08:38.460 --> 01:08:39.860
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Mr. Chair, part of...

asr-000982
01:08:39.860 --> 01:08:49.980
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Part po ng activities that the DFA will conduct is yung training and information dissemination po.

asr-000983
01:08:49.980 --> 01:08:55.860
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: So yung pagpapaintindi po sa ating mga kababayan, how important their vote is.

asr-000984
01:08:56.580 --> 01:09:08.480
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: So yun po yung nagdodouble efforts yung DFA and of course in partnership with COMELEC to educate our mga kababayan overseas po.

asr-000985
01:09:08.820 --> 01:09:08.980
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: So that...

asr-000986
01:09:09.860 --> 01:09:15.720
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Yun po yung way na ma-increase po yung turnout natin, Mr. Chair.

asr-000987
01:09:15.720 --> 01:09:25.080
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: And of course, better accessibility to the information needed through postings not only sa consular offices,

asr-000988
01:09:25.260 --> 01:09:36.240
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: I mean sa foreign posts offices, but also through the direct communication with our recorded kababayans, Mr. Speaker.

asr-000989
01:09:37.000 --> 01:09:39.720
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: As you know, Mr. Speaker, 2288 is around...

asr-000990
01:09:39.860 --> 01:09:49.400
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So do you think the 18% will translate maybe half, maybe 50% kaya ba natin by 2028?

asr-000991
01:09:49.880 --> 01:10:05.540
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Otherwise, Mr. Speaker, sayang lang yung pondong ibinibigay natin because we're funding our massive information campaign for our kababayan overseas to make sure na makaboto sila because every vote counts.

asr-000992
01:10:05.540 --> 01:10:08.540
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So do you see in the 20...

asr-000993
01:10:09.860 --> 01:10:16.680
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Or maybe the presidential election, tataas ang ating turnout vote?

asr-000994
01:10:17.840 --> 01:10:24.240
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: That is the hope and the direction, Mr. Speaker, na mapapataas po yung rate.

asr-000995
01:10:24.460 --> 01:10:36.720
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: And of course, we also are expecting that the COMELEC will double its efforts in increasing the turnout rate, Mr. Speaker.

asr-000996
01:10:36.720 --> 01:10:39.720
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: But as far as the DFA is concerned...

asr-000997
01:10:39.860 --> 01:10:47.840
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: In coordinating with the overseas Filipino voters, so they're doubling their efforts already po, Mr. Speaker.

asr-000998
01:10:47.840 --> 01:10:50.760
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you for that, good sponsor.

asr-000999
01:10:50.880 --> 01:10:55.340
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Mr. Speaker, may I go to one of the crucial mandates of the department?

asr-001000
01:10:56.280 --> 01:11:08.120
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Mr. Speaker, distinguished sponsor, can you confirm the report that DFA had already lodged 39 diplomatic protests against China in 2026?

asr-001001
01:11:08.120 --> 01:11:14.050
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: And 296 from 2022 through 2026?

asr-001002
01:11:14.620 --> 01:11:16.380
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Yes, that is correct, Mr. Speaker.

asr-001003
01:11:17.840 --> 01:11:28.720
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: The diplomacy program itself is seeking approximately 14.48 billion in 2027. Is this correct?

asr-001004
01:11:29.820 --> 01:11:31.340
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Yes, Mr. Speaker, that's correct.

asr-001005
01:11:31.340 --> 01:11:39.340
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: For the next fiscal year, or maybe for the past years, what performance framework does DFA use to determine...

asr-001006
01:11:39.860 --> 01:11:45.720
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: ...whether these protests are producing the intended diplomatic outcome?

asr-001007
01:11:46.980 --> 01:12:01.140
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Mr. Speaker, we believe that these diplomatic protests, since these are legal documents, have in a way toned down the aggression of other countries against the Philippines, Mr. Speaker.

asr-001008
01:12:02.740 --> 01:12:09.140
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Makikita naman po natin na yung DFA, it is their role...

asr-001009
01:12:09.860 --> 01:12:21.380
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: ...is to diplomatically negotiate and communicate with other countries, Mr. Chair.

asr-001010
01:12:21.800 --> 01:12:39.240
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: So, as we see na ngayon, while tensions are still there, pero medyo in a controlled level na po, then that is already an achievement on the part of the DFA, Mr. Chair, na yung mga inisyo na diplomatic notes are effective.

asr-001011
01:12:39.240 --> 01:12:39.740
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: And in fact...

asr-001012
01:12:39.860 --> 01:12:44.900
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: And in fact, many of which have been answered by China, Mr. Chair.

asr-001013
01:12:45.180 --> 01:12:51.540
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Yung iba, maramihan po nila sinagot. Yung iba po, isa-isa nila sinagot.

asr-001014
01:12:53.140 --> 01:12:55.800
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Mr. Speaker, Distinguished Sponsor.

asr-001015
01:12:55.800 --> 01:13:09.800
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Is DFA tracking, for example, whether a protest receives a formal response, whether the complaint of conduct ceases or recurs, whether partner governments...

asr-001016
01:13:09.860 --> 01:13:21.800
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: ...issues, supporting statements, whether operational behavior at sea changes, otherwise our protest will just be a mere formality with no outcome?

asr-001017
01:13:23.940 --> 01:13:30.700
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: As mentioned, Mr. Chair, there is no one-on-one, one-to-one correspondence on our protests with China.

asr-001018
01:13:32.540 --> 01:13:38.700
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Yung reply nila, minsan, there are three or four diplomatic notes and they will only reply with one...

asr-001019
01:13:39.860 --> 01:13:43.300
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: They will reply to that once, yung three or four diplomatic notes.

asr-001020
01:13:43.880 --> 01:13:57.140
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: And we can see now, Mr. Chair, humuhupuan naman po yung tensyon as far as yung mga naririnig natin sa news before na there's attack against our fishermen, against our Coast Guard.

asr-001021
01:13:57.140 --> 01:14:09.140
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: So ngayon, we are seeing na medyo nagto-tone down po, Mr. Chair, and we believe that this is greatly due also to the diplomatic notes issue.

asr-001022
01:14:09.860 --> 01:14:12.460
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: by the Department of Foreign Affairs, Mr. Chair.

asr-001023
01:14:12.840 --> 01:14:15.240
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Mr. Speaker, Distinguished Sponsor.

asr-001024
01:14:15.920 --> 01:14:34.160
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: This becomes more relevant because on September 11, following a Philippine Coast Guard report that Chinese forces fired flares toward a Philippine aircraft near Zamora, Subi, and Panganiban Mischief Reefs.

asr-001025
01:14:34.320 --> 01:14:38.280
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: The FBI public called on China to cease its activities.

asr-001026
01:14:39.860 --> 01:14:47.800
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: at the futures and reiterated its position under UNCLOS and the 2016 Arbitral Award.

asr-001027
01:14:48.720 --> 01:14:49.280
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Is this correct?

asr-001028
01:14:50.500 --> 01:14:51.760
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Yes, Mr. Chair, that's correct.

asr-001029
01:14:53.020 --> 01:14:58.680
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So with respect to the September flare incident, did DFA lodge a diplomatic protest?

asr-001030
01:15:00.000 --> 01:15:12.080
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Mr. Chair, the DFA is about to send a diplomatic protest on that particular attack, Mr. Chair.

asr-001031
01:15:12.440 --> 01:15:15.140
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, it happened last week, September 11.

asr-001032
01:15:15.320 --> 01:15:15.920
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Yes, Mr. Chair.

asr-001033
01:15:15.920 --> 01:15:21.420
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, isn't it after the incident, the following day, we should launch a protest?

asr-001034
01:15:21.540 --> 01:15:24.360
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Hindi ba ganun ang SOP natin dyan?

asr-001035
01:15:24.700 --> 01:15:26.280
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Not immediately, Mr. Speaker.

asr-001036
01:15:26.280 --> 01:15:38.760
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Because the DFA awaits the detailed incident report about the attacks before they send out a diplomatic protest, Mr. Speaker.

asr-001037
01:15:39.920 --> 01:15:41.400
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: So, we're just going to wait.

asr-001038
01:15:42.040 --> 01:15:47.600
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: So, in short, we are about to send one already, Mr. Speaker.

asr-001039
01:15:48.180 --> 01:15:49.760
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: So, hindi na po magtatagal.

asr-001040
01:15:49.940 --> 01:15:51.960
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, are we expecting this week or next week?

asr-001041
01:15:53.020 --> 01:15:56.260
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Once the complete report has been submitted.

asr-001042
01:15:56.280 --> 01:15:59.620
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Once the complete report has been submitted to the office already, Mr. Speaker,

asr-001043
01:15:59.900 --> 01:16:04.860
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: then immediately, that diplomatic note will be sent out.

asr-001044
01:16:06.020 --> 01:16:08.300
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Mr. Speaker, Distinguished Sponsor.

asr-001045
01:16:08.920 --> 01:16:15.220
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: I'll go to the funding for the Consular and Assistance to Nationals, yung tinatawag natin ATN program.

asr-001046
01:16:16.280 --> 01:16:25.580
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Is it correct that the Consular and ATN program goes from approximately 7.47 billion in 2026

asr-001047
01:16:26.280 --> 01:16:31.880
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: to 13.63 billion in 2027, an 82.4% increase?

asr-001048
01:16:31.880 --> 01:16:33.360
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Can you enlighten us?

asr-001049
01:16:33.960 --> 01:16:38.160
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: What's this Assistance to Nationals program?

asr-001050
01:16:39.820 --> 01:16:40.800
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Yes, Mr. Speaker.

asr-001051
01:16:42.380 --> 01:16:47.920
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: The Assistance to Nationals program, as for the Assistance to Nationals program,

asr-001052
01:16:48.480 --> 01:16:51.680
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: there is a proposed funding for 2027.

asr-001053
01:16:54.640 --> 01:16:55.880
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: And yet, Mr. Speaker, Distinguished Sponsor,

asr-001054
01:16:56.280 --> 01:17:02.100
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: in 2025, the program obligated 65% of its appropriations

asr-001055
01:17:02.100 --> 01:17:05.200
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: and disbursed only 38%.

asr-001056
01:17:05.200 --> 01:17:10.540
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: What exactly will an additional 6.6 billion purchase

asr-001057
01:17:10.540 --> 01:17:13.940
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: that the department could not deliver with its previous budget?

asr-001058
01:17:14.660 --> 01:17:17.040
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Which line item will benefit from this increase?

asr-001059
01:17:17.300 --> 01:17:23.300
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Remember yung absorptive capacity nyo, utilization rate, mababa,

asr-001060
01:17:23.420 --> 01:17:24.800
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: and then you're asking for more?

asr-001061
01:17:24.800 --> 01:17:25.960
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Mr. Speaker,

asr-001062
01:17:26.280 --> 01:17:29.740
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: we are talking about the Assistance to Nationals program.

asr-001063
01:17:30.020 --> 01:17:34.740
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Mr. Speaker, the Assistance to Nationals program

asr-001064
01:17:34.740 --> 01:17:38.920
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: is like an insurance fund na gagamitin lang po kung kailangan.

asr-001065
01:17:39.060 --> 01:17:42.800
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: It does not necessarily mean that if the proposed budget is

asr-001066
01:17:42.800 --> 01:17:47.660
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: for discussions purposes, 1 billion,

asr-001067
01:17:47.840 --> 01:17:51.040
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: kailangan ubusin po yan on that fiscal year.

asr-001068
01:17:51.040 --> 01:17:56.040
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Because it depends upon, it will depend upon the needs and the requests for assistance.

asr-001069
01:17:56.280 --> 01:18:00.000
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: From Filipinos overseas, Mr. Chair.

asr-001070
01:18:00.140 --> 01:18:07.840
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: So, masasabi po natin, the lower the rate of utilization,

asr-001071
01:18:08.920 --> 01:18:13.940
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: masasabi po natin, it's better for us kasi ibig sabihin lang po nun,

asr-001072
01:18:14.320 --> 01:18:17.360
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: konti lang po yung mga kababayan natin na nangangilangan ng tulong

asr-001073
01:18:17.360 --> 01:18:21.580
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: and pumunta po sa atin, sa DFA, para humihingi po ng tulong, Mr. Chair.

asr-001074
01:18:21.580 --> 01:18:25.000
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, insured, Mr. Speaker, insured, that's part of insurance.

asr-001075
01:18:25.120 --> 01:18:25.900
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Yun ba yung gusto nyo?

asr-001076
01:18:26.280 --> 01:18:29.360
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Yes, Mr. Speaker. It's like an insurance fund, Mr. Speaker.

asr-001077
01:18:29.360 --> 01:18:32.540
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, you're asking for more because parang standby siya for insurance?

asr-001078
01:18:32.740 --> 01:18:36.380
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Yes, Mr. Speaker. Kasi yung prior years po, mababalik na po sa National Treasury.

asr-001079
01:18:36.680 --> 01:18:45.420
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Okay. But, is it, I thought, yung 5.2 billion is increase in home office for MOOE.

asr-001080
01:18:46.200 --> 01:18:49.340
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Yun ba yun? So, it's not going to insurance?

asr-001081
01:18:49.340 --> 01:18:49.520
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Yes.

asr-001082
01:18:52.760 --> 01:18:56.260
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Mr. Speaker, yung nire-request po ng DFA,

asr-001083
01:18:56.280 --> 01:19:03.860
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: na ATN fund is around 1 billion annually and around 200 million for the Legal Assistance Fund.

asr-001084
01:19:04.420 --> 01:19:05.280
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Legal Assistance Fund.

asr-001085
01:19:06.520 --> 01:19:06.760
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Okay.

asr-001086
01:19:07.300 --> 01:19:11.960
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, how about MOOE nyo? Parang tumaas din ng 5.2 billion?

asr-001087
01:19:12.020 --> 01:19:26.160
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Mr. Speaker, yung sinasabi pong 5.8 billion budget is for the passport procurement and production, Mr. Speaker.

asr-001088
01:19:26.280 --> 01:19:26.780
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Yeah.

asr-001089
01:19:27.480 --> 01:19:42.040
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Mr. Speaker, sponsor, could you explain the breakdown of the 13 billion, the share of passport, production, ordinary consular operations, ATN, legal assistance, reputation, ICT, and so on and so forth?

asr-001090
01:19:42.820 --> 01:19:45.680
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Ano itong breakdown ng 13 billion? Just to be transparent.

asr-001091
01:19:48.300 --> 01:19:49.220
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Mr. Speaker,

asr-001093
01:19:55.150 --> 01:19:56.220
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: we're just reviewing the breakdown.

asr-001094
01:19:56.280 --> 01:19:56.840
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Okay, Mr. Speaker.

asr-001095
01:20:16.420 --> 01:20:25.020
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Mr. Speaker, ang tinatanong po ng Butihing Kalihim ay yung breakdown po ng 13.8 billion. Tama po ba?

asr-001096
01:20:25.120 --> 01:20:25.400
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Yes.

asr-001099
01:20:46.420 --> 01:21:10.900
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Mr. Speaker, 12.4 billion will go to the consular services, Mr. Speaker.

asr-001100
01:21:10.900 --> 01:21:15.260
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: So, kasama na po yan yung passport production,

asr-001101
01:21:15.260 --> 01:21:21.180
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: yung issuance of apostille certificates, among others, Mr. Speaker.

asr-001102
01:21:23.660 --> 01:21:27.180
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Mr. Speaker, good sponsor.

asr-001103
01:21:27.820 --> 01:21:30.260
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: In relation to the budget of ATN,

asr-001104
01:21:31.600 --> 01:21:41.500
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: DFA explained in the previous committee briefing that part of the law ATN utilization is attributable to the creation of the Department of Migrant Workers

asr-001105
01:21:41.500 --> 01:21:45.240
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: and the transfer of OFW-related assistance functions.

asr-001106
01:21:45.260 --> 01:21:46.360
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Is this correct?

asr-001107
01:21:46.360 --> 01:21:59.540
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: That's correct, Mr. Speaker, kasi yung DMW po, na-devolved na po doon yung ATN funds for overseas Filipino workers or for OFWs po.

asr-001108
01:21:59.540 --> 01:22:13.900
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: What remains under the umbrella of the DFA are overseas Filipinos who are not working abroad,

asr-001109
01:22:13.900 --> 01:22:15.100
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: such as tourists,

asr-001110
01:22:15.100 --> 01:22:23.700
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Students, dual citizens who in case of emergencies nangangailangan po ng tulong, Mr. Speaker.

asr-001111
01:22:24.060 --> 01:22:33.540
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: And also in some areas where there are no DMW satellite offices yet, Mr. Speaker.

asr-001112
01:22:34.300 --> 01:22:42.460
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: So yung DFA pa rin po yung tumutugon sa mga pangangailangan po ng mga OFWs in those particular areas, Mr. Speaker.

asr-001113
01:22:42.460 --> 01:22:45.360
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Please walk me through.

asr-001114
01:22:45.880 --> 01:22:53.140
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Ibang DMW natin sa mga consular natin o embassy, meron ba silang satellite office inside ng ano nyo o wala?

asr-001115
01:22:53.500 --> 01:22:59.460
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Mr. Speaker, hindi po lahat ng may DFA offices may DMW.

asr-001116
01:23:00.700 --> 01:23:10.740
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: So as of now, there are only 48 DMW satellite offices, Mr. Speaker.

asr-001117
01:23:10.740 --> 01:23:11.740
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Inside the embassy.

asr-001118
01:23:12.460 --> 01:23:13.720
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Ganun ba yun yung consular nyo? Ganun ba yun?

asr-001119
01:23:14.200 --> 01:23:14.840
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: It's separate.

asr-001120
01:23:16.540 --> 01:23:21.580
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Or they have a office, small office inside your consular or your ano?

asr-001121
01:23:22.700 --> 01:23:26.340
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Marami po sa kanila, Mr. Speaker, are together inside the embassy.

asr-001122
01:23:26.520 --> 01:23:32.960
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: But there are also areas where DMW is renting or leasing their offices outside po.

asr-001123
01:23:33.460 --> 01:23:39.640
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Do you think that the law utilization because of overlapping, meron ba yung overlapping with DMW when it comes to ATN?

asr-001124
01:23:39.640 --> 01:23:42.240
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Mr. Speaker, lalabas po na.

asr-001125
01:23:42.460 --> 01:24:05.580
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Overlapping in terms of yung line item but yung mga tao na kinikater, again, DMW caters to OFWs po, yung DFA, yung mga Filipinos who are overseas but are not necessarily workers and OFWs who are in areas without any DMW offices, Mr. Speaker.

asr-001126
01:24:06.300 --> 01:24:08.620
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Mr. Speaker, Distinguished Sponsor.

asr-001127
01:24:08.620 --> 01:24:12.440
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: I have more few questions but because my time is winding down.

asr-001128
01:24:12.460 --> 01:24:17.340
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: I just want to follow the strict rule of 30 minutes so this will be my last questions.

asr-001129
01:24:18.340 --> 01:24:26.240
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Recently, our good Secretary of Foreign Affairs, Guibo Chidoro, attended an international forum abroad.

asr-001130
01:24:26.920 --> 01:24:34.920
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Siguro ay napanood na natin ito lahat because this becomes viral not only here but also internationally.

asr-001131
01:24:34.920 --> 01:24:42.040
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Sa video na ito, makikita natin na may nag-abot ng note habang si Secretary Guibo ay nagsasalita.

asr-001132
01:24:42.460 --> 01:25:04.580
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: At habang siya ay may sinasagot na tanong on stage, Secretary Guibo, upon reading the note, stopped mid-sentence at binasa niya ang nilalaman ng note na ito na nanggaling umano sa China, allegedly from China, Chinese Embassy representatives present in the forum.

asr-001133
01:25:04.580 --> 01:25:11.580
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: As we saw later in the photos, naglalaman ito ng pag-atake ng China sa 2016.

asr-001134
01:25:12.460 --> 01:25:15.880
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: South China Sea Arbitration Ruling.

asr-001135
01:25:16.640 --> 01:25:25.820
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Inawag itong iligal at ang desisyon ng UNCLOS Arbitration Tribunal ay paglabag raw sa international law.

asr-001136
01:25:26.720 --> 01:25:39.840
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Secretary Guibo called this stealthy passing of the note as actual coercion, bullying, and aggression, and a sign of disrespect towards South Korea as the host.

asr-001137
01:25:39.840 --> 01:25:39.920
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you very much.

asr-001138
01:25:42.460 --> 01:25:52.160
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Mr. Speaker, this is your sponsor. May we ask the official position of the Department of Foreign Affairs on this incident?

asr-001139
01:25:53.500 --> 01:26:02.420
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Mr. Speaker, the Department of Foreign Affairs respects the statements and views of the good Secretary of the Department of National Defense.

asr-001140
01:26:02.880 --> 01:26:10.800
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: However, it maintains that it will continue to deal with these aggressions diplomatically, Mr. Speaker.

asr-001141
01:26:10.800 --> 01:26:10.840
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Thank you.

asr-001142
01:26:12.460 --> 01:26:17.040
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Mr. Speaker, are you going to file also a protest or you will lodge a protest?

asr-001143
01:26:17.400 --> 01:26:28.500
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Mr. Speaker, hinihintay pa po ng opisina yung buong detalye po from the incident, Mr. Speaker.

asr-001144
01:26:28.720 --> 01:26:31.460
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So eventually, are you going to lodge a protest?

asr-001145
01:26:32.020 --> 01:26:39.040
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: It will depend upon the evaluation po, Mr. Speaker, on our DFA officials.

asr-001146
01:26:39.040 --> 01:26:42.040
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: If it is necessary to issue a diplomatic...

asr-001147
01:26:42.460 --> 01:26:44.500
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: A diplomatic note on that matter, Mr. Speaker.

asr-001148
01:26:44.500 --> 01:26:49.000
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So in short, yung evaluation nyo, is this an act of aggression yung ginawa?

asr-001149
01:26:49.200 --> 01:26:57.620
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Because during a forum, may biglang aabot sa'yo, that's seldom, peculiar na makikita nyo.

asr-001150
01:26:58.180 --> 01:27:03.200
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So I think this is something that we have to file a protest, no?

asr-001151
01:27:03.280 --> 01:27:04.680
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Kasi hindi maganda yung ginawa.

asr-001152
01:27:05.280 --> 01:27:11.560
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: No less than, we were insulted, you know, because Secretaries, the alter ego of our President,

asr-001153
01:27:12.460 --> 01:27:13.720
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: yung nakakaya itong ginawa.

asr-001154
01:27:15.580 --> 01:27:16.680
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Yes, Mr. Speaker.

asr-001155
01:27:16.980 --> 01:27:24.860
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: But the DFA maintains its stand that differences in position are better addressed through established diplomatic channels

asr-001156
01:27:24.860 --> 01:27:32.600
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: and in a manner consistent with the courtesy and professionalism expected in official international engagements, Mr. Speaker.

asr-001157
01:27:33.420 --> 01:27:35.780
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Thank you, Mr. Speaker. I have no more questions.

asr-001158
01:27:38.180 --> 01:27:39.100
Deputy Speaker Yasser Alonto Balindong: Majority Leader.

asr-001159
01:27:40.140 --> 01:27:41.780
Rep. Patricia C. Calderon: Mr. Speaker, next to interpolate.

asr-001160
01:27:42.460 --> 01:27:47.920
Rep. Patricia C. Calderon: The sponsor, I move to recognize Representative Rene Luisco of Kabataan Partylist.

asr-001161
01:27:48.860 --> 01:27:53.200
Deputy Speaker Yasser Alonto Balindong: The Honorable Rene Luisco is recognized to interpellate the sponsor.

asr-001162
01:27:54.440 --> 01:27:55.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Thank you, Mr. Speaker.

asr-001163
01:27:56.340 --> 01:28:00.740
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And good morning to the distinguished sponsor and, of course, to the department.

asr-001164
01:28:01.960 --> 01:28:08.780
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: My first question is to clarify whether, to clarify the mandate of the DFA.

asr-001165
01:28:09.380 --> 01:28:10.620
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Please correct me if I'm wrong.

asr-001166
01:28:11.440 --> 01:28:12.300
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Tama po ba that the DFA...

asr-001167
01:28:12.460 --> 01:28:22.360
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: The DFA acts as the primary coordinator, advisor, and processing agency for the negotiation, ratification, and entry into force of treaties in the Philippines,

asr-001168
01:28:22.900 --> 01:28:30.460
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: supposedly determining whether an international agreement qualifies as an executive agreement or a treaty requiring legislative concurrence

asr-001169
01:28:31.000 --> 01:28:41.000
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: and drafting and coordinating closely with its offices on the drafts of the ratification of such treaties.

asr-001170
01:28:41.000 --> 01:28:42.000
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: I'm sure that the DFA...

asr-001171
01:28:42.980 --> 01:28:44.040
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: has many mandates.

asr-001172
01:28:44.340 --> 01:28:50.580
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: But may I request from the sponsor to clarify if this is accurate.

asr-001173
01:28:51.020 --> 01:28:52.480
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam, Mr. Speaker, good sponsor.

asr-001174
01:28:53.220 --> 01:28:54.880
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Yes, Mr. Speaker, that is correct.

asr-001175
01:28:55.440 --> 01:29:03.720
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Mr. Speaker, good sponsor, I ask this because I'd like to clarify our commitments in relation to the Basel Convention.

asr-001176
01:29:04.320 --> 01:29:10.800
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: We ratified the Basel Convention already in 1993, a few years after we signed it in 1989.

asr-001177
01:29:11.120 --> 01:29:12.440
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: But on the 5th of

asr-001178
01:29:12.460 --> 01:29:14.460
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: December 2019, the

asr-001179
01:29:14.460 --> 01:29:16.340
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Basel Ban Amendment became

asr-001180
01:29:16.340 --> 01:29:18.580
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: international law and was adopted

asr-001181
01:29:18.580 --> 01:29:20.360
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: by the parties to the Basel

asr-001182
01:29:20.360 --> 01:29:22.460
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Convention back

asr-001183
01:29:22.460 --> 01:29:24.600
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: in 1995. May we

asr-001184
01:29:24.600 --> 01:29:26.200
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: ask for an update on the

asr-001185
01:29:26.200 --> 01:29:28.520
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: ratification of the Basel Ban Amendment?

asr-001186
01:29:42.460 --> 01:29:47.060
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Mr. Speaker,

asr-001187
01:29:47.500 --> 01:29:49.060
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: the Department is currently

asr-001188
01:29:49.060 --> 01:29:50.700
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: checking on the status of the

asr-001189
01:29:50.700 --> 01:29:52.080
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: and updates of the ratification.

asr-001190
01:29:53.840 --> 01:29:55.080
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: But it

asr-001191
01:29:55.080 --> 01:29:58.340
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: is

asr-001192
01:29:58.340 --> 01:29:59.860
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: under the

asr-001193
01:30:00.000 --> 01:30:11.300
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: under the view of the DFA that this is under the Department of Environment and National Resources, Mr. Speaker?

asr-001194
01:30:11.860 --> 01:30:14.480
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Yes, Madam Speaker. Mr. Speaker, good sponsor.

asr-001195
01:30:15.200 --> 01:30:22.220
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: We also asked the DNR on the update on the ratification of the Basel ban amendment.

asr-001196
01:30:22.700 --> 01:30:28.140
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: In 2020, they said it's in the works and six years later, this year,

asr-001197
01:30:28.140 --> 01:30:31.320
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: we are given essentially the same update.

asr-001198
01:30:31.860 --> 01:30:42.180
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So, given that there's almost no movement as to how we are compliant with this international agreement that we entered into,

asr-001199
01:30:42.600 --> 01:30:48.000
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: what can the DFA do to ensure that action and follow-through happens

asr-001200
01:30:48.000 --> 01:30:53.780
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: so that this agreement has translation in ratification?

asr-001201
01:30:54.260 --> 01:30:55.280
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Mr. Speaker, good sponsor.

asr-001202
01:30:55.280 --> 01:30:58.120
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Mr. Speaker, upon checking, the DFA has ratified.

asr-001203
01:30:58.140 --> 01:31:01.960
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: The DFA has ratified the main agreement but not the protocols, Mr. Speaker.

asr-001204
01:31:02.380 --> 01:31:09.960
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: So, it is only the main agreement which is necessary to be ratified by the DFA.

asr-001205
01:31:10.360 --> 01:31:15.360
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: And the DFA will coordinate with the DNR as to the status of the protocols.

asr-001206
01:31:16.060 --> 01:31:22.220
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So, to clarify, we're talking about the Basel ban amendment and this is separate from the convention?

asr-001207
01:31:22.440 --> 01:31:23.660
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Yes, that's correct, Mr. Speaker.

asr-001208
01:31:23.660 --> 01:31:27.660
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Okay. Mr. Speaker, good sponsor, we'd like to request a report.

asr-001209
01:31:28.140 --> 01:31:37.480
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: We'd like to request a report on how the DFA has ratified the Basel ban amendment already

asr-001210
01:31:37.480 --> 01:31:43.680
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: and is waiting on the protocols which I understand is with the DNR. Is this correct?

asr-001211
01:31:44.060 --> 01:31:45.480
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Yes, Mr. Speaker, that is correct.

asr-001212
01:31:45.780 --> 01:31:54.920
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: And the DFA would willingly submit a report to the Office of the Good Congressman whenever it is ready, Mr. Speaker.

asr-001213
01:31:54.920 --> 01:31:56.920
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Even if there is no...

asr-001214
01:31:58.140 --> 01:32:02.720
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: defined, definitive update yet on the protocols.

asr-001215
01:32:03.320 --> 01:32:08.420
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: I raise this, Mr. Speaker, good sponsor because under the Basel Convention,

asr-001216
01:32:08.660 --> 01:32:11.720
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: which we already ratified and it's already enacted into law,

asr-001217
01:32:12.320 --> 01:32:17.640
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: state parties like the Philippines cannot trade waste with non-parties

asr-001218
01:32:17.640 --> 01:32:22.500
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: unless there is a bilateral agreement with that non-party

asr-001219
01:32:22.500 --> 01:32:28.060
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: which has terms and protections equal or better than that provided in the Basel Convention.

asr-001220
01:32:28.140 --> 01:32:36.040
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And in the past year, however, there's been more than 250 shipments of electronic waste

asr-001221
01:32:36.040 --> 01:32:39.560
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: from the United States imported by the Philippines.

asr-001222
01:32:40.040 --> 01:32:46.520
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And the United States is a non-party to the Basel Convention which makes these imports illegal.

asr-001223
01:32:46.920 --> 01:32:49.820
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Is the DFA aware of this, Mr. Speaker, good sponsor?

asr-001224
01:32:51.020 --> 01:32:56.820
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Mr. Speaker, the DFA is not aware of the information being...

asr-001225
01:32:58.140 --> 01:33:00.140
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: presented by the good congressman.

asr-001226
01:33:01.120 --> 01:33:02.420
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Mr. Speaker, good sponsor.

asr-001227
01:33:03.040 --> 01:33:11.480
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: We are sharing this because this is a violation of our commitments to the international community of states

asr-001228
01:33:11.480 --> 01:33:16.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: which we say, you know, that when we'd like to regulate the trade of waste,

asr-001229
01:33:16.700 --> 01:33:24.000
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: that should happen amongst parties and should there be trade with non-parties,

asr-001230
01:33:24.220 --> 01:33:27.760
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: that should be the subject of an agreement.

asr-001231
01:33:28.140 --> 01:33:35.640
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Which, again, should have protections equal or greater than that that we've already entered into.

asr-001232
01:33:35.640 --> 01:33:44.960
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: But, so I'd like to ask, is the DFA aware of any movements to have a bilateral treaty

asr-001233
01:33:44.960 --> 01:33:53.500
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: that would allow the imports by the Philippines of electronic waste or waste from the United States?

asr-001234
01:33:54.000 --> 01:33:57.360
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Mr. Speaker, as of the moment, the DFA is not aware of any.

asr-001235
01:33:58.140 --> 01:34:03.580
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Bilateral agreements or any planned revision of our existing laws.

asr-001236
01:34:03.800 --> 01:34:11.300
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: And the DFA will look into the matter being raised by our good colleague, Mr. Speaker,

asr-001237
01:34:11.300 --> 01:34:18.660
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: and evaluate on kung sino po ang dapat managot if there are violations, Mr. Speaker.

asr-001238
01:34:19.300 --> 01:34:20.480
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Mr. Speaker, good sponsor.

asr-001239
01:34:20.640 --> 01:34:27.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: This is also a multi-layered issue that we'd also ask these questions to,

asr-001240
01:34:28.140 --> 01:34:30.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: the SBMA, the Subic Bay Metropolitan Authority,

asr-001241
01:34:30.700 --> 01:34:38.400
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: on which these electronic wastes are currently entering into our jurisdiction,

asr-001242
01:34:39.000 --> 01:34:42.040
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: also the Bureau of Customs, also the DNR.

asr-001243
01:34:42.140 --> 01:34:46.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: But it is in our due diligence that we're also asking the DFA

asr-001244
01:34:46.700 --> 01:34:50.100
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: because regardless of whether there is such an agreement

asr-001245
01:34:50.100 --> 01:34:52.480
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: or whether there are plans for such an agreement,

asr-001246
01:34:53.160 --> 01:34:56.020
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: these shipments are already here and they're illegal.

asr-001247
01:34:56.020 --> 01:34:57.440
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And we don't know.

asr-001248
01:34:58.140 --> 01:35:00.080
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Kung saan na pupunta itong electronic waste,

asr-001249
01:35:00.200 --> 01:35:01.320
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: ano pong ginagawa nito,

asr-001250
01:35:01.760 --> 01:35:05.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: kung naka-expose po sila sa kalupaan natin,

asr-001251
01:35:06.020 --> 01:35:08.020
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: na-expose to the elements,

asr-001252
01:35:08.180 --> 01:35:11.240
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: anong pinapasok nito sa groundwater natin,

asr-001253
01:35:11.360 --> 01:35:12.500
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: sa shores natin, etc.

asr-001254
01:35:13.380 --> 01:35:17.780
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Worse, if there is such a bilateral agreement in the future,

asr-001255
01:35:18.180 --> 01:35:22.060
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: if signed, it would directly undermine the Basel Ban Amendment,

asr-001256
01:35:22.500 --> 01:35:24.160
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Article 4A of that convention,

asr-001257
01:35:24.160 --> 01:35:28.080
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: which the Philippines already signed and has provided already,

asr-001258
01:35:28.140 --> 01:35:31.180
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: ratified, at hinihintay na lang po kung paano ma-enact

asr-001259
01:35:31.180 --> 01:35:32.160
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: and tuloy yung protocols.

asr-001260
01:35:33.040 --> 01:35:34.840
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Specifically, it says that

asr-001261
01:35:34.840 --> 01:35:40.480
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: any member state of the OECD, European Union, or Liechtenstein

asr-001262
01:35:40.480 --> 01:35:43.880
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: are disallowed from exporting hazardous wastes

asr-001263
01:35:43.880 --> 01:35:46.600
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: to countries outside of that group.

asr-001264
01:35:47.160 --> 01:35:49.960
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And the Basel parties have not ruled on whether Article 11

asr-001265
01:35:49.960 --> 01:35:53.680
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: could be used to undermine another convention article itself.

asr-001266
01:35:54.360 --> 01:35:56.180
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So, Madam Speaker, good sponsor,

asr-001267
01:35:56.180 --> 01:35:58.120
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: or we'd like to put this in the chat box,

asr-001268
01:35:58.120 --> 01:36:00.140
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: but on record, if there are any movements

asr-001269
01:36:00.140 --> 01:36:02.000
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: to make this kind of arrangement,

asr-001270
01:36:02.620 --> 01:36:06.240
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: the export of wastes from the United States

asr-001271
01:36:06.240 --> 01:36:09.260
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: to the Philippines, or our import thereof,

asr-001272
01:36:09.580 --> 01:36:12.160
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: legal, via bilateral agreement or treaty,

asr-001273
01:36:12.560 --> 01:36:16.260
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: the DFA is mandated to ensure that it doesn't happen

asr-001274
01:36:16.260 --> 01:36:19.360
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: because it is in contravention to the existing agreements

asr-001275
01:36:19.360 --> 01:36:20.820
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: we've already entered into.

asr-001276
01:36:21.300 --> 01:36:23.420
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So, Madam Speaker, Mr. Speaker, good sponsor,

asr-001277
01:36:23.420 --> 01:36:26.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: as a last question, do we have DFA's commitment to ensure

asr-001278
01:36:26.700 --> 01:36:27.960
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: that we do not enter?

asr-001279
01:36:28.120 --> 01:36:29.780
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And do we have any bilateral agreement

asr-001280
01:36:29.780 --> 01:36:32.320
